SRC/bog -- changes made for the OSK freeware collection  mkdict.c, 2026-09-26.  It read each line with gets() into a buffer one  word long (MAXWORDLEN + 1), so any line longer than 40 characters ran  over it -- a 240-character line stopped it with a bus error.  It reads  with fgets() now, into a buffer one byte longer for the newline, and  passes over a line too long to be a word, the way it passes over any  line it cannot use.  The dictionary it makes from GAMES/words is  byte-for-byte the GAMES/BOG/dict that ships.  The original is  mkdict.c.ori; rebuilt -qm from recipe `mkdict'.